+++ b/native/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# smallpt browser port
+
+Based on Kevin Beason’s MIT-licensed smallpt:
+https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
+
+`smallpt-original.cpp` is the upstream source. `smallpt.cpp` retains its ray/sphere intersections, diffuse/specular/refractive materials, Russian roulette, camera, and Cornell box scene. The adaptation exports setup, framebuffer, and progressive row rendering functions instead of writing a PPM from main. It accumulates four samples per pixel per pass, with gamma correction for display. The palette tints the two foreground spheres and their corresponding walls. The light remains neutral.
+
+Run `npm run build:wasm` with Emscripten (`em++`) on PATH. The resulting ES module and `.wasm` binary are committed under `public/wasm`, so ordinary `npm run build` does not require the compiler. All live tracing runs in a module Web Worker, without pthreads or SharedArrayBuffer headers. New renders terminate the previous worker, so stale frames cannot overwrite the new scene. Errors are displayed in the canvas status bar.
+
+`npm run build:preview` uses native g++ and Sharp to generate the initial poster from this same renderer. It does not start a server. The live WebAssembly render replaces the poster as samples arrive.
+
+The home page is prerendered as `index.html`, including the canvas and controls. The rest of the existing Astro app retains its server adapter.
+
+Upstream license: `LICENSE.txt`.
